---
// Version anglaise de src/pages/politique-de-protection-des-donnees.astro.
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Data protection policy | digitags.work"
  description="digitags.work data protection policy: data collected, cookies, rights of access, rectification and erasure (GDPR)."
>
  <section class="page-hero" style="padding-bottom: 20px;">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1>The Hub's data protection policy</h1>
      <p class="lead">We take data protection seriously.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="container prose">
    <h2>Introduction</h2>
    <p>digitags.work is committed to protecting the privacy of all visitors to www.digitags.work. This privacy statement covers our practices in relation to our website. It is designed to help you understand how we collect, use and safeguard the personal information you provide to us, and to help you make informed decisions when using our site and services. digitags.work fully respects your right to privacy: we do not collect any personal information about you when you visit our site, unless you choose to provide it through one of our forms.</p>
    <p>By using this site, you consent to the collection and use of your information under the terms of this statement, in accordance with the Data Protection Acts 1988 to 2018, the ePrivacy Regulations 2011, and the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR).</p>
    <p>We update this policy regularly: please check it from time to time.</p>

    <h2>Information we collect</h2>
    <p>In the course of operating our website, we may collect and process the following data about you:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Details of your visits to our site and the resources you access (traffic data, pages viewed, communication data), as well as the information you provide to us when listing your profile on the platform. All IP addresses are anonymised: no information can be linked to a visitor of the site.</li>
      <li>The data provided when you sign up or when you communicate with us through our contact forms or the "I'm a freelancer" button.</li>
    </ul>
    <div style="overflow-x: auto;">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Type of collection</th><th>Categories</th><th>Details</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td rowspan="2">Provided by the freelancer</td><td>Personal information</td><td>First name, last name, email</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Professional information</td><td>Role, specialty, portfolio, professional references, willingness to appear in newsletters or on the site, CV (document provided by the freelancer)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Generated by your use of the site</td><td>Browsing data</td><td>Necessary cookies and, subject to your consent, other cookies and IP address</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2>Use of cookies</h2>
    <h3>What are cookies?</h3>
    <p>Like most professional websites, this site may use cookies — small files downloaded to your computer — to improve your experience. This section describes the information they collect, how we use them and why we sometimes need to store them, as well as how to prevent them from being stored (which may, however, degrade certain features of the site).</p>
    <h3>Disabling cookies</h3>
    <p>You can prevent cookies from being set by adjusting your browser settings (see its help section for how to do so). Disabling cookies may affect certain features of this site and of many other sites you visit.</p>
    <h3>Third-party cookies</h3>
    <p>When an audience measurement solution is used (such as Google Analytics), it helps us understand how you use the site in order to improve your experience: time spent on the site, pages visited. All IP addresses are anonymised at collection, so that no data can be linked to a visitor, thereby guaranteeing your privacy.</p>

    <h2>Use of your information</h2>
    <p>The information we collect and store is mainly used to provide you with our services (offering you freelance missions, and our newsletters). We may also use it for the following purposes:</p>
    <p><strong>For freelancers:</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Allowing the digitags.work teams to check whether your profile may suit the missions proposed by our clients;</li>
      <li>Contacting you where appropriate;</li>
      <li>Proposing and sharing your profile with clients who may be interested in your services;</li>
      <li>Featuring your profile (limited information: first name, last name, role, main references), if you have authorised us to do so via the relevant checkbox on the sign-up form, in our newsletters presenting the latest profiles to join.</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>For prospects:</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Contacting you when you have expressed a need;</li>
      <li>Sharing the latest news about digitags.work with you.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Disclosure of your information</h2>
    <p>Where applicable, we may disclose your personal information to any member of our group (subsidiaries, holding company and its other subsidiaries, where relevant). We may also disclose your personal information to third parties in the event of a legal claim. <strong>We do not sell your data.</strong></p>

    <h2>Third-party links</h2>
    <p>You may find links to third-party websites on our site. These sites have their own privacy policies, which we invite you to review. We accept no responsibility for their practices, over which we have no control.</p>

    <h2>Access to your information</h2>
    <p>Your data is only accessible to digitags.work, as data controller, for the purposes for which you provide it. You have the right to request a copy of the personal data we hold about you; we will provide it within 30 days.</p>

    <h2>Right to erasure of your data</h2>
    <p>You can request the deletion of your data at any time by writing to <a href="mailto:contactme@dgitags.com">contactme@dgitags.com</a>. We will delete it within 36 hours and confirm by email.</p>

    <h2>Right to rectification of your data</h2>
    <p>You can request changes to your data at any time by writing to <a href="mailto:contactme@dgitags.com">contactme@dgitags.com</a>.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions about this privacy policy are welcome: through our <a href="/en/contact">contact form</a> or directly at <a href="mailto:contactme@dgitags.com">contactme@dgitags.com</a>.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
